  {
    "full_slug": "posts/typed-content-from-storyblok",
    "name": "Typed content from a headless CMS",
    "content": {
      "component": "post",
      "title": "Typed content from a headless CMS",
      "excerpt": "Why generating one PHP class per component beats passing arrays around, and what it costs you.",
      "published_at": "2026-11-09 08:00",
      "author": "{{uuid:authors/sample-author}}",
      "categories": [
        "{{uuid:categories/storyblok}}",
        "{{uuid:categories/php}}"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "php",
        "storyblok"
      ],
      "body": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Most headless CMS integrations start the same way: a decoded JSON array, a few null checks and a template that quietly knows too much about the shape of the data. It works until the content model changes."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Start with the content model"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Components in the CMS are the contract. If each one becomes a class, the contract is visible to your editor, to static analysis and to the next person reading the template."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "blok",
            "attrs": {
              "id": null,
              "body": [
                {
                  "component": "code_block",
                  "filename": "app/Http/Controllers/PostController.php",
                  "language": "php",
                  "code": "$story = $storyblok->stories()\n    ->bySlug('posts/'.$slug, PostTransfer::class);\n\n$title = $story?->getContent()->getTitle();"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "blok",
            "attrs": {
              "id": null,
              "body": [
                {
                  "component": "callout",
                  "label": "// note",
                  "text": "Everything except arrays is nullable, so templates need the nullsafe operator or a fallback."
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Resolve relations once"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Relations arrive next to the content, not inside it. Look them up once per request and pass the result down, instead of asking in every partial."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "blok",
            "attrs": {
              "id": null,
              "body": [
                {
                  "component": "pull_quote",
                  "text": "The template should read like a description of the page, not a negotiation with the API."
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Keep the glue small"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Every workaround you write is a suggestion for the package. Write it down while it is still annoying."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "seo_title": "Typed content from a headless CMS · your-blog",
      "seo_description": "Why generating one PHP class per component beats passing arrays around, and what it costs you."
    }
  },
  {
    "full_slug": "posts/caching-published-reads",
    "name": "Caching published reads without surprises",
    "content": {
      "component": "post",
      "title": "Caching published reads without surprises",
      "excerpt": "Fresh windows, stale fallbacks and when a webhook should purge what.",
      "published_at": "2026-11-02 08:00",
      "author": "{{uuid:authors/sample-author}}",
      "categories": [
        "{{uuid:categories/laravel}}",
        "{{uuid:categories/tooling}}"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "laravel",
        "cache"
      ],
      "body": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Published content changes rarely and is read constantly, which makes it a good fit for a short cache. The interesting part is what happens when the refresh fails."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A store of its own"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Give Storyblok a dedicated cache store. Clearing it from a webhook empties the whole store, so it must not share a store with sessions or anything else."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "blok",
            "attrs": {
              "id": null,
              "body": [
                {
                  "component": "code_block",
                  "filename": "config/cache.php",
                  "language": "php",
                  "code": "'storyblok' => [\n    'driver' => 'file',\n    'path' => storage_path('framework/cache/storyblok'),\n],"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "blok",
            "attrs": {
              "id": null,
              "body": [
                {
                  "component": "callout",
                  "label": "// heads up",
                  "text": "Drafts are never cached, so editors see their changes immediately in a preview environment."
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Stale is better than down"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A stale copy can be served for up to a day if a refresh fails. For a blog that is the right trade: a slightly old post beats an error page."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "seo_title": "Caching published reads without surprises · your-blog",
      "seo_description": "Fresh windows, stale fallbacks and when a webhook should purge what."
    }
  },
  {
    "full_slug": "posts/richtext-with-embedded-blocks",
    "name": "Rendering richtext with embedded blocks",
    "content": {
      "component": "post",
      "title": "Rendering richtext with embedded blocks",
      "excerpt": "Walking the richtext tree, rendering nested components and deriving heading anchors.",
      "published_at": "2026-10-24 08:00",
      "author": "{{uuid:authors/sample-author}}",
      "categories": [
        "{{uuid:categories/storyblok}}",
        "{{uuid:categories/laravel}}"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "blade",
        "storyblok"
      ],
      "body": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Storyblok richtext is a tree. Paragraphs, headings and lists are nodes, and editors can insert whole components between them."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Walk the tree yourself"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A small recursive renderer is enough: plain nodes become HTML, and component nodes dispatch to a Blade component named after the block."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "blok",
            "attrs": {
              "id": null,
              "body": [
                {
                  "component": "code_block",
                  "filename": "resources/views/components/blocks/callout.blade.php",
                  "language": "blade",
                  "code": "@props(['label' => '// note', 'text' => ''])\n<aside class=\"callout\">\n    <div class=\"label\">{{ $label }}</div>\n    <p>{{ $text }}</p>\n</aside>"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Anchors and the index"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Heading ids and the on-this-page index come from the same walk: collect every level-two heading, slugify its text, and render both."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "blok",
            "attrs": {
              "id": null,
              "body": [
                {
                  "component": "pull_quote",
                  "text": "One pass over the document, three outputs: HTML, anchors and read time."
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "seo_title": "Rendering richtext with embedded blocks · your-blog",
      "seo_description": "Walking the richtext tree, rendering nested components and deriving heading anchors."
    }
  },
  {
    "full_slug": "posts/blade-components-for-blocks",
    "name": "One Blade component per block",
    "content": {
      "component": "post",
      "title": "One Blade component per block",
      "excerpt": "Mapping CMS block names to anonymous components and keeping the mapping honest.",
      "published_at": "2026-10-12 08:00",
      "author": "{{uuid:authors/sample-author}}",
      "categories": [
        "{{uuid:categories/laravel}}"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "blade"
      ],
      "body": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A block named code_block in the CMS maps to a Blade component with the same name. No registry, no switch statement, just a naming rule."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The naming rule"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Anonymous components live in resources/views/components/blocks. The renderer builds the component name from the block name and skips anything it does not recognise."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "blok",
            "attrs": {
              "id": null,
              "body": [
                {
                  "component": "callout",
                  "label": "// rule",
                  "text": "Unknown blocks are skipped, not fatal. An editor adding a new block type should never take the page down."
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "seo_title": "One Blade component per block · your-blog",
      "seo_description": "Mapping CMS block names to anonymous components and keeping the mapping honest."
    }
  },
  {
    "full_slug": "posts/sitemaps-from-the-links-endpoint",
    "name": "Sitemaps from the links endpoint",
    "content": {
      "component": "post",
      "title": "Sitemaps from the links endpoint",
      "excerpt": "A sitemap that costs one request instead of one per story.",
      "published_at": "2026-10-03 08:00",
      "author": "{{uuid:authors/sample-author}}",
      "categories": [
        "{{uuid:categories/laravel}}",
        "{{uuid:categories/tooling}}"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "seo",
        "laravel"
      ],
      "body": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A sitemap needs a path and a date for every page, not every page's content. The links endpoint returns exactly that."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "One request"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Ask the links endpoint for everything under posts and map each entry to a url element. The result fits comfortably in a short cache."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "blok",
            "attrs": {
              "id": null,
              "body": [
                {
                  "component": "code_block",
                  "filename": "routes/web.php",
                  "language": "php",
                  "code": "Route::get('/sitemap.xml', SitemapController::class);"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "seo_title": "Sitemaps from the links endpoint · your-blog",
      "seo_description": "A sitemap that costs one request instead of one per story."
    }
  },
